  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative or low (e.g., < 0.33) to counteract overconfidence.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes (last 5-7 days) when sentiment is positive, to avoid lagged reactions.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is > 10% above recent 30-day average, reduce by 5-10% unless sentiment strongly bullish.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp upward moves (e.g., > 5% spike in 3-5 days) by 10-20% to avoid overcorrection.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.33–0.67), align forecast with historical volatility range (±15% of 30-day mean) to avoid extreme deviations.",
    "For long-term horizons (>14 days), apply a 2-3% downward bias to account for market stabilization and regulatory adjustments."
  ]
